From 4bdb0c12a2132b8f7d5fff8c17dae09e05000267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukin <mylukin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 09:08:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 57/98] fix(plugins): prevent late plugin reloads from
 destroying global hook runner

maybeBootstrapChannelPlugin and other runtime provider registries call
loadOpenClawPlugins(activate:true) with a different cache key than
gateway startup, triggering a full registry rebuild that replaces the
global hook runner.  The new registry lacks hooks registered during
startup (e.g. message_received from feishu_chat), silently dropping
all group messages.

Layer 1: maybeBootstrapChannelPlugin now returns early when any channel
plugins are already loaded, preventing the most common trigger.

Layer 2: initializeGlobalHookRunner carries forward hooks (and their
plugin records) from the previous registry when the new one lacks them,
guarding against ALL activate:true callers.  The merged registry is a
shallow copy to avoid polluting the loader cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
